From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjcoggan <hjcoggan2@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:51:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 25/35] cmake: align Android ELF segments to 16 KB

Android 15 devices can use 16 KB pages, and the loader then refuses segments
aligned to 4 KB. -Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384 produces binaries that work on
both; from codepdbh/nfsmw-android sdk/ (BSD-3-Clause), CMakeLists.txt.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 38daaac..a9b70b2 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -174,6 +174,10 @@ elseif(ANDROID)
     endif()
     # include/rex/platform.h sets REX_PLATFORM_ANDROID (and REX_PLATFORM_LINUX)
     # from __ANDROID__; nothing is added here so the two cannot disagree.
+    # 16 KB page-size devices (Android 15+): align ELF segments so the same
+    # libraries load on 4 KB and 16 KB kernels. Consumers linking the SDK as a
+    # subdirectory should set this for their own targets as well.
+    add_link_options("-Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384")
 elseif(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
     if(REX_TARGET_PROCESSOR MATCHES "AMD64|x86_64")
         set(REX_PLATFORM "linux-amd64")
